<p>The Pentagon has named four U.S. Army Reserve soldiers killed when a drone strike hit a command center at a U.S. base in Kuwait, according to multiple outlets covering the announcement. The soldiers were Capt. Cody A. Khork; Sgt. 1st Class Noah L. Tietjens; Sgt. 1st Class Nicole M. Amor; and Sgt. Declan J. Coady—troops described as working in logistics and sustainment roles supporting deployed forces and tied to a unit associated with the 103rd Sustainment Command out of Des Moines, Iowa. U.S. Central Command says six American service members have been killed so far in the U.S.-Iran conflict. The BBC described the Kuwait drone strike as the first U.S. fatalities in the fighting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_sdvGKCbwfC-i2VdUv4kjdr-aV2ddG9EzBE5BK55gudKnsRlcHjpQsV3q3Ira6Z1qTk1Eo_2h_Y_IDoNefw_M4fViQK-CCBjKguD5DvJtPLh9e1Oc3UTp4E29z0G4u11T3-If0FGYqkjRurdLTO5F32dYUshEQ4UKZ74P54R0v9lPYMp8cfemXafYPi4hEuuFN8Z32pIlWtLvOlHP4oWsCBbkYfaLABw6Jehtd8YfcLU4zr0LhUMUHy0wfZw7fTUvBXuSZay1aIsPjOcDw' alt='Declan Coady poses for a photo on graduation day at Fort Sill in March 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Site detail: Reports said the strike hit a command center on a U.S. base in Kuwait, and coverage cited U.S. officials who described it as a drone attack.</li><li>Unit and hometowns: Reuters reported the soldiers were Army Reserve members tied to the 103rd Sustainment Command out of Des Moines, Iowa. It also listed their home communities as Winter Haven, Florida (Khork); Bellevue, Nebraska (Tietjens); White Bear Lake, Minnesota (Amor); and West Des Moines, Iowa (Coady).</li><li>Age range: The BBC said the four identified service members ranged in age from 20 to 42.</li><li>Evacuation mechanics: Rubio said the U.S. is using larger commercial flights, charter flights, military transportation, and land routes to help Americans leave the region as the war spreads.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon: The Defense Department named four of the six Americans killed, describing them as Army Reservists from different states whose logistics work helped keep forces supplied; it had not yet released the other two names. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/pentagon-identifies-4-of-6-u-s-soldiers-killed-in-iran-war-by-drone-strike-in-kuwait'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump called the fallen “true American patriots” and said he expected additional U.S. casualties before the war ends. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/03/pentagon-us-soldiers-kuwait-strike'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>U.S. State Department: Rubio said officials were looking for additional flights and routes to move Americans out as the war spreads to neighboring countries, amid market anxiety and surging oil prices. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-03-0800/middle-east-us-iran-war-live-updates-pentagon-identifies-us-soldiers-killed-kuwait-strike'>AllSides</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-iran-war-middle-east-conflict-who-are-the-first-four-us-soldiers-killed-in-iran-conflict-11166128#publisher=newsstand'>Who Were The First Four US Soldiers Killed In Iran Strikes</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/pentagon-identifies-4-of-6-u-s-soldiers-killed-in-iran-war-by-drone-strike-in-kuwait'>Pentagon identifies 4 of 6 U.S. soldiers killed in Iran war by drone strike in Kuwait</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq33ynl07o'>First US soldiers to die in Iran conflict are identified</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pentagon-identifies-first-us-soldiers-killed-iran-war'>Pentagon identifies first US soldiers killed in Iran war</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/03/pentagon-us-soldiers-kuwait-strike'>Pentagon names four of six US soldiers killed in Iranian strike on Kuwait base</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a 